)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Held Output Panel                        !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}
}  The Held Output panel (H) lists the jobs that have held output, the
}  output that is not printed until it is released. Here you look at
}  the output of jobs whose MSGCLASS is a held class, for example.
}  The oldest comes first, by the time the job ended.
}
}  H alone shows the jobs whose names begin with your user id. H ALL
}  shows all you may see (topic 13 of the contents); PREFIX takes the
}  place of your user id. DEST limits the list as well.
}
}  Action characters:
{   ?  }Show the job's data sets (Job Data Set panel).
{   S  }Browse the job's output (Output Data Set panel).
{   O  }Release the held output for printing ($O). With a new DEST typed
}       over the field, it goes there ($R first).
}  A new DEST without O: "O" ACTION REQUIRED. To purge, use P on ST.
}
}  Type the number of a topic, or press Enter to see them in order.
@     1 }The H command: classes, ALL and a job name
@     2 }The fields of the panel
@     3 }Commands on the list panels
}  Enter: topic 1   PF7: contents   PF10: back   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZSEL = TRANS(&ISFHCMD
                 1,ISFHHQC
                 2,ISFHHQF
                 3,ISFHLSM
                *,'?')
  &ZCONT = ISFHHQC
  &ZUP = ISFHTOC
)END
